      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/6252354d464db3c645186b9a8ef6001ee76408b04f7abf6a9046656270607085.png)\n\nFor the pentagon above, determine the measure of the exterior angle of $∠B.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let us call $z$ the exterior angle of $∠B.$ Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{50}^{∘}+z+{80}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{100}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {280}^{∘}+z & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
