      "dom_id": "step-q68128",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/b98ac3a59b0726c47d273b06891f9aeabcb0b31c9e5937887464fec0205cb677.png)\n\nFind the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(x-{8}^{∘})+(2x+{4}^{∘})+(2x-{14}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x-{18}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={378}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={63}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
