      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193271/assets/409b89d99c494f3273ce228ebb828e440a3c5ab4940344e775680225eed84d8b.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+(x+{40}^{∘})+(3x-{40}^{∘})+3x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 9x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
